# p_7e4a — Water Bottle at the Nightstand in the Morning; Sometimes Stays Home on Workdays (fork of p_8e1b)

This fork of p_8e1b addresses two anomalies in the water bottle's behaviour. First, on day 8 at 12:00 (weekday, within the 9–14 work window), the water bottle was sighted at nightstand_b1 — directly contradicting the parent's OUT_OF_HOUSE prediction. Second, the per-object stats show the water bottle at 5 different receptacles across 9 sighted days, with counter_k1 on only 2/9 days. This is a highly mobile object.

The interpretation: Mara's morning routine involves the water bottle in the bedroom (she drinks from it in bed or at the nightstand before getting up). It sits at the nightstand from roughly 6:00 to 8:00. Then she either takes it with her to the co-working space (most days) or leaves it on the counter (some days, perhaps when she is running late or the co-working space has its own water). The 12:00 nightstand sighting on day 8 is an outlier — perhaps she forgot it, or it is a home-work day.

What changed from p_8e1b: (1) water_bottle_mara gains a "both 6–8.5h at nightstand_b1" block (morning bedroom routine). (2) The OUT_OF_HOUSE block for weekday 8.5–14.5 is downgraded from "usually" to "sometimes" (the bottle does not always travel). (3) A "both 8.5–14.5 at counter_k1" block is added as the in-house alternative when the bottle stays home. (4) The claim now tests the nightstand location in the morning.

What sets this apart from p_8e1b: at 7:00 on a weekday, the water bottle is at the nightstand (not the counter); during weekday 9–14, it may be at the counter (not always OUT_OF_HOUSE). What would refute it: the water bottle found at the counter at 7:00 on a weekday, or the water bottle found at the nightstand during weekday 10–13 on multiple occasions.

