# p_d4a1 — Water Bottle is Mobile: Nightstand Only Rarely Before 6:00 (fork of p_c9d2)

This fork of p_c9d2 weakens the water-bottle-at-nightstand prediction. The parent's nightstand claim (4–6h, "sometimes") has 3 for but 6 against — more than half the looks in that window find the bottle elsewhere. The per-object statistics show water_bottle_mara at 6 distinct receptacles, with nightstand_b1 holding only 3/12 sighted days. The bottle is genuinely mobile: it travels with Mara to the co-working space on most weekday mornings, sits at the counter when she is home, and occasionally rests at the nightstand while she is in bed. The nightstand is not the bottle's "home" — it is a transient resting spot.

What changed from p_c9d2: (1) The nightstand block's chance is lowered from "sometimes" to "rarely" — the bottle is at the nightstand only on a minority of early-morning looks. (2) The claim is retained but the document's prose acknowledges the low confidence. (3) All other blocks (counter default, OUT_OF_HOUSE weekday, evening kitchen table) are unchanged.

