This fork of p_f6b3 softens the phone's weekday OUT_OF_HOUSE block from "usually" to "sometimes." The parent's claim "phone is out of the house during weekday work hours" has scored for 0, against 3, weak for 3 across the full log. The per-object data shows phone_mara at nightstand_b1 on 7/11 sighted days, and weekday 9–17h looks at the nightstand found the phone 4 times versus 6 empty. That 4/10 in-house rate during work hours is far too high for a "usually out" prediction. Mara's phone is her primary communication device and she likely leaves it at the nightstand (charging) on many workdays, taking it only on days she needs it at the co-working space. The laptop, charger, and glasses travel more reliably; the phone is the one item that stays.

What changed from p_f6b3: (1) phone_mara OUT_OF_HOUSE weekday 8.5–14.5 changed from "usually" to "sometimes." (2) The phone OUT_OF_HOUSE claim is replaced with a phone-at-nightstand weekday 9–14h claim, testing that the phone stays home during work hours. (3) The weekend morning claim and tablet claim are unchanged.

