# p_c7e4 — Jacket Stays at the Entry Hook in the Evening; Wallet at Entry Table (fork of p_d4a1)

This fork of p_d4a1 removes the jacket-at-chair_k1 and wallet-at-chair_k2 evening blocks that have been failing across the entire library. The jacket claim "at chair_k1 17–23h" has scored for 1, against 8 in p_d4a1 (and identically in p_c9d2, p_a4f7, p_5d8b, p_f3a9, p_b2f8). The per-object data confirms jacket_mara is at entry_hook_e1 on 4/9 sighted days (its "mostly" location) with 5 distinct receptacles, and the wallet_mara is at entry_table_e1 on 8/11 sighted days. The "evening drop zone at the chairs" hypothesis inherited from p_5d8b is simply wrong: Mara hangs her jacket back on the entry hook when she comes home, and her wallet goes to the entry table. The chair_k1 and chair_k2 sightings are rare exceptions (perhaps she sits in a chair and sets them down momentarily), not the default.

What changed from p_d4a1: (1) Removed the jacket_mara chair_k1 17–23h "sometimes" block; the jacket stays at entry_hook_e1 all day. (2) Removed the wallet_mara chair_k2 17–23h "sometimes" block; the wallet stays at entry_table_e1 all day. (3) The jacket claim now tests entry_hook_e1 17–23h. (4) The wallet claim now tests entry_table_e1 17–23h. (5) All other blocks (water bottle, glasses, work-day OUT_OF_HOUSE) are unchanged.

What sets this apart from p_d4a1: at 19:00, the jacket is at entry_hook_e1 (not chair_k1) and the wallet is at entry_table_e1 (not chair_k2). What would refute it: the jacket consistently found at chair_k1 during 17–23h, or the wallet at chair_k2 during that window.

